{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>YHWH desired, etc.</b> This is so that He would not look to show the justice of HaShem until He makes His Torah great, so that all who forsake it would fear; or this verse may be joined with what comes after it, for HaShem showed His justice, and this is the people who say about the prophet that he is blind, that he is despised and rejected:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {0 "Bracketed [דבק] supplied from context; the word appears to be missing or implied in the manuscript."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:37.364805051Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}